Frequently Asked Interview Question
Difference between orElse() and orElseGet()
Optional<String> name = Optional.of("Sunil");

System.out.println(
        name.orElse(getDefaultName())
);

getDefaultName() executes even when the value exists.

Optional<String> name = Optional.of("Sunil");

System.out.println(
        name.orElseGet(() -> getDefaultName())
);

getDefaultName() executes only when the Optional is empty.

Interview Answer
Optional.of() → Value must not be null.
Optional.ofNullable() → Value may be null.
isPresent() → Check existence.
ifPresent() → Execute if value exists.
orElse() → Return default value.
orElseGet() → Lazily generate default value.
orElseThrow() → Throw exception if empty.
map() → Transform Optional value.
filter() → Apply condition on Optional value.


